          <details class="code-toggle">
            <summary>Voir snippet</summary>
            <pre class="code-block">METHOD calc_next_delivery.
  READ ENTITIES OF zi_coffee_sub_trl IN LOCAL MODE
    ENTITY zi_coffee_sub_trl
    FIELDS ( start_date next_delivery_date status )
    WITH CORRESPONDING #( keys )
    RESULT DATA(lt_sub).
  DATA lt_upd TYPE TABLE FOR UPDATE zi_coffee_sub_trl.
  LOOP AT lt_sub ASSIGNING FIELD-SYMBOL(&lt;s&gt;).
    IF &lt;s&gt;-start_date IS INITIAL OR &lt;s&gt;-start_date = '00000000'.
      CONTINUE.
    ENDIF.
    "si deja CANCELED, ne plus recalculer
    IF &lt;s&gt;-status = 'CANCELED'.
      CONTINUE.
    ENDIF.
    DATA lv_next TYPE d.
    lv_next = &lt;s&gt;-start_date + 2.
    "Decaler si week-end (6=sam / 7=dim)
    DATA(lv_wd) = weekday( lv_next ).
    IF lv_wd = 6.
      lv_next = lv_next + 2.
    ELSEIF lv_wd = 7.
      lv_next = lv_next + 1.
    ENDIF.
    IF &lt;s&gt;-next_delivery_date &lt;&gt; lv_next.
      APPEND VALUE #( %tky = &lt;s&gt;-%tky next_delivery_date = lv_next ) TO lt_upd.
    ENDIF.
  ENDLOOP.

  IF lt_upd IS NOT INITIAL.
    MODIFY ENTITIES OF zi_coffee_sub_trl IN LOCAL MODE
      ENTITY zi_coffee_sub_trl
      UPDATE FIELDS ( next_delivery_date )
      WITH lt_upd.
  ENDIF.

ENDMETHOD.

  METHOD weekday.
    IF iv_date IS INITIAL OR iv_date = '00000000'.
      rv_wd = 1.
      RETURN.
    ENDIF.
    DATA lv TYPE string.
    lv = |&amp;#123; iv_date &amp;#125;|. "YYYYMMDD
    DATA y TYPE i.
    DATA m TYPE i.
    DATA d TYPE i.
    y = lv(4).
    m = lv+4(2).
    d = lv+6(2).
    IF m &lt; 1 OR m &gt; 12.
      rv_wd = 1.
      RETURN.
    ENDIF.
    DATA t TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF i WITH EMPTY KEY.
    t = VALUE #( ( 0 ) ( 3 ) ( 2 ) ( 5 ) ( 0 ) ( 3 ) ( 5 ) ( 1 ) ( 4 ) ( 6 ) ( 2 ) ( 4 ) ).
    IF m &lt; 3.
      y = y - 1.
    ENDIF.
    DATA idx TYPE i.
    idx = m. "1..12
    DATA w TYPE i.
    w = ( y + y / 4 - y / 100 + y / 400 + t[ idx ] + d ) MOD 7.
    IF w = 0.
      rv_wd = 7.
    ELSE.
      rv_wd = w.
    ENDIF.
  ENDMETHOD.</pre>
          </details>
          <details class="code-toggle">
            <summary>Voir explication</summary>
            <div class="muted">Les d&eacute;terminations dans SAP RAP</div>
            <div class="muted">R&ocirc;le des d&eacute;terminations</div>
            <div class="muted">
              Les d&eacute;terminations permettent d&rsquo;enrichir ou d&rsquo;ajuster automatiquement les donn&eacute;es
              d&rsquo;un objet m&eacute;tier, sans bloquer l&rsquo;utilisateur.
            </div>
            <div class="muted">
              Contrairement aux validations, une d&eacute;termination :
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>ne bloque pas l&rsquo;enregistrement,</li>
              <li>est d&eacute;clench&eacute;e automatiquement par le framework,</li>
              <li>sert &agrave; calculer, compl&eacute;ter ou synchroniser des champs.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="muted">
              Elles sont id&eacute;ales pour appliquer des r&egrave;gles m&eacute;tier implicites, qui ne
              n&eacute;cessitent pas d&rsquo;intervention utilisateur.
            </div>
            <div class="muted">Place des d&eacute;terminations dans l&rsquo;architecture RAP</div>
            <div class="muted">
              Les d&eacute;terminations font partie du Behavior Definition (BDEF) et sont ex&eacute;cut&eacute;es :
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>lors de la cr&eacute;ation d&rsquo;un draft,</li>
              <li>lors de la modification de certains champs,</li>
              <li>avant l&rsquo;activation de l&rsquo;objet.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="muted">
              Elles s&rsquo;ex&eacute;cutent &agrave; l&rsquo;int&eacute;rieur du cycle draft, ce qui garantit que les
              donn&eacute;es actives sont toujours coh&eacute;rentes.
            </div>
            <div class="muted">O&ugrave; d&eacute;finir les d&eacute;terminations</div>
            <div class="muted">1. Behavior Definition (BDEF)</div>
            <div class="muted">Les d&eacute;terminations sont d&eacute;clar&eacute;es dans la Behavior Definition :</div>
            <pre class="code-block">determination set_defaults on modify &#123; create; &#125;</pre>
            <div class="muted">
              Cette d&eacute;claration indique :
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>quand la d&eacute;termination est d&eacute;clench&eacute;e,</li>
              <li>dans quel contexte (create / modify),</li>
              <li>et sur quel &eacute;v&eacute;nement.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="muted">2. Behavior Implementation (classe ZBP_*)</div>
            <div class="muted">La logique est impl&eacute;ment&eacute;e dans la classe de comportement :</div>
            <pre class="code-block">METHOD set_defaults.
  IF status IS INITIAL.
    status = 'NEW'.
  ENDIF.

  IF delivery_frequency IS NOT INITIAL.
    next_delivery_date = sy-datum + 30.
  ENDIF.
ENDMETHOD.</pre>
